    <briefdescription>
<para>A unified matrix type for representing images, kernels, or other arbitrary matrix-like structures. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Rows are stored consecutively, with channels belonging to the same element stored next to one another. The address of row <computeroutput>r</computeroutput> is: <computeroutput>(uint8_t *)mat-&gt;<ref refid="structcvl___mat_1a7ea2fa4d4e1adbd98db38c5b857c7525" kindref="member">data</ref> + r * mat-&gt;<ref refid="structcvl___mat_1a0d6019dc9e366139d2989f2062c22139" kindref="member">stride</ref></computeroutput>.</para>
<para>The same type represents both images and other matrix data, such as floating-point kernels. For example, an 8-bit image and a 64-bit kernel are both <ref refid="structcvl___mat" kindref="compound">cvl_Mat</ref>, distinguished by <computeroutput><ref refid="structcvl___mat_1a71cb86901a271fe1741559382302bcb4" kindref="member">depth</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="structcvl___mat_1a8cedab15dca04a2465cf1c35f3c807cc" kindref="member">channels</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
